ity whose progress the watchdog timer checks.  In kernel and user
tickle modes, an attempt is made to refresh the watchdog timer in
one half the timer’s configured  period.   For  example,  if  the
watchdog  timer  has a period of 30 seconds, a refresh attempt is
made every 15 seconds.  If called without  arguments,  will  list
the  timers  available  on  the  system.   When arming a watchdog
timer, the argument is the name of the timer to  arm.   Only  one
timer  may  be  armed  at  a time; if an attempt is made to arm a
timer when one is already armed, an error message  will  be  dis‐
